ogeneous impact of conditional cash transfers","a":["Sebastian Galiani","Patrick J. McEwan"],"y":2013,"c":"pub","j":"Journal of Public Economics","v":"103","p":"85-96","r":23,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpubeco.2013.04.004","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1016/j.jpubeco.2013.04.004"},{"t":"The effects of quantitative skills training on college outcomes and peers","a":["Kristin F. Butcher","Patrick J. McEwan","Corrine H. Taylor"],"y":2010,"c":"pub","j":"Economics of Education Review","v":"29","i":"2","p":"187-199","r":61,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.econedurev.2009.06.001","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1016/j.econedurev.2009.06.001"},{"t":"The Benefits of Delayed Primary School Enrollment: Discontinuity Estimates Using Exact Birth Dates","a":["Patrick J. McEwan","Joseph S. Shapiro"],"y":2008,"c":"pub","j":"Journal of Human Resources","v":"43","i":"1","p":"1-29","r":25,"l":"https://doi.org/10.3368/jhr.43.1.1","lt":"pub","doi":"10.3368/jhr.43.1.1"},{"t":"The Central Role of Noise in Evaluating Interventions That Use Test Scores to Rank Schools","a":["Kenneth Y Chay","Patrick J Mcewan","Miguel Urquiola"],"y":2005,"c":"pub","j":"American Economic Review","v":"95","i":"4","p":"1237-1258","r":0,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1257/0002828054825529","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1257/0002828054825529"},{"t":"Peer effects on student achievement: evidence from Chile","a":["Patrick J. McEwan"],"y":2003,"c":"pub","j":"Economics of Education Review","v":"22","i":"2","p":"131-141","r":61,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0272-7757(02)00005-5","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1016/s0272-7757(02)00005-5"}]